1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,793
Someone offered Lucia cash to remember a
sunset she'd never seen. Jason

2
00:00:04,793 --> 00:00:06,790
thought yes would cost nothing.

3
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:11,582
The man played a video: orange water, a
blue railing, himself smiling

4
00:00:11,582 --> 00:00:13,180
beside an empty chair.

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:18,365
He wanted her to say she'd sat there
yesterday. One harmless sentence, he

6
00:00:18,365 --> 00:00:19,960
said, sliding over money.

7
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:24,752
Lucia knew the terrace. Its railing had
been repainted white last month.

8
00:00:24,752 --> 00:00:26,350
The man stopped smiling.

9
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:31,144
Jason looked at the envelope, then
video. Somebody else might pay for

10
00:00:31,144 --> 00:00:33,940
their convenient memory with years
behind bars.

11
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:39,132
He pushed the cash back. The man called
them ungrateful and walked away

12
00:00:39,132 --> 00:00:40,330
without another word.

13
00:00:40,330 --> 00:00:45,516
They bought one coffee to share beneath
the real white railing while rain

14
00:00:45,516 --> 00:00:47,910
erased the last orange light offshore.

15
00:00:47,910 --> 00:00:53,019
Jason raised the cup toward the empty
chair. That one sentence, Lucia

16
00:00:53,019 --> 00:00:56,000
said, would have belonged to somebody
forever.
